# The base store is a BUILD PRODUCT, not an artefact: it is rebuilt from the
# committed records in 1.1 s, and it is 13 MB.  The MEASUREMENTS beside it are
# committed, because those are what a later reader cannot regenerate without
# the gitignored `library/`.
store.jsonl
store.jsonl.gz

# ⚠️ AND THE `.json` SPELLING, because the 2026-09-17 handoff's own command
# wrote `--out store.json` -- which the two names above do not match on the
# EXTENSION, so a 9 MB build product sat one `git add` from the tree. The CLI
# says "write the base store (JSONL) here" and the file IS JSONL, so `.json`
# is the wrong spelling rather than a second format; ignored so that either
# spelling is safe.
store.json
store-two-publishers.jsonl

# ⚠️ AND THE RECORDS THEMSELVES (140-423 MB). The convention is
# `library/_shared-records/` -- machine-local, md5-receipted, read by explicit
# path -- so a record written here by the handoff's command is a DUPLICATE of
# the shared copy, not a second artefact. See IDENTITY_RUN_2026-09-17.md.
*.record.json
